{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/793401-sfx-help","id":793401,"title":"Sfx Help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-26T20:56:00-08:00","id":793401,"title":"Sfx Help","content":"I need help finding embeds that mechanically accomplish some of the classic espionage-thriller storybeats.<ul><li>You spot someone across the street, watching you. A bus drives past, obscuring your vision for a few seconds. Then, they're gone.</li> <li>You chase a person to a roof edge... and they throw themselves from the edge, as you rush to the edge, they're gone, and the people below are walking by obliviously, no sign of a splattered body, no one clinging to the wall.</li> <li>Someone walks into a dark church. All the candles in the place flicker to life.</li> </ul><br /> I'd prefer embeds to exploits or form-powers, as my chronicle already has a bit of a running gag that 4 Minutes Ago accomplishes everything. If there's no alternative option, eh, I'll live.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T04:25:44-08:00","id":793507,"title":"","content":"Here's the notes on a Embed I was prototyping:<ul><li><b><u>Blink of the Eye</u></b> (Mundane): The Demon exploit quantum uncertainty to change their location from one unobserved spot to another.</li> <li><u>Dice Pool</u>: Dexterity + Athletics<ul><li><u>Dramatic Failure</u>: The Demon glitches out their movement, appearing in someone\u2019s view and provoking Compromise.</li> <li><u>Failure</u>: The Demon fails to shift locations.</li> <li><u>Success</u>: The Demon \u201cvanishes\u201d from one spot to appear at another unobserved location within double their Speed + Successes.</li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Exceptional Success</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Extra successes are their own reward? Allow movement even when observed (and random coincidence breaks observation for a moment).</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul>The idea was to exploit Uncertainty to allow for the Demon to appear anywhere else they <i>could</i> be in range (like with In My Pocket, and the presence/absence of small items, but here with the Demon's location). The main issue I was trying to decide was:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Prevent the Demon for using it when observed or to observed locations? But that serves to tell the Demon they are under observation, and/or the target location is.</li> <li>Just force Compromise if they are under active observation. But that can get pretty punishing since it isn't easy to tell the observational states of themselves and another location. Though I guess other Embeds and Exploits might help with that.</li> </ol><br /> Using the above Embed (once finished), after line of sight is broken by the bus, the target uses to Embed to shift a short distance away, then leaves the area by traditional means. Same with going over the ledge.<br /> <hr />As for the candles trick, Combustion, maybe? Make the wicks <i>really</i> flammable, so that a minor air pressure change or vibration sets them burning?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 12-27-2015, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T04:28:13-08:00","id":793510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/793401-sfx-help#post793401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need help finding embeds that mechanically accomplish some of the classic espionage-thriller storybeats.<ul><li>You spot someone across the street, watching you. A bus drives past, obscuring your vision for a few seconds. Then, they're gone.</li> <li>You chase a person to a roof edge... and they throw themselves from the edge, as you rush to the edge, they're gone, and the people below are walking by obliviously, no sign of a splattered body, no one clinging to the wall.</li> <li>Someone walks into a dark church. All the candles in the place flicker to life.</li> </ul><br /> I'd prefer embeds to exploits or form-powers, as my chronicle already has a bit of a running gag that 4 Minutes Ago accomplishes everything. If there's no alternative option, eh, I'll live.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. This is probably the most difficult, but you could use something along the lines of &quot;Never here&quot; &quot;Lost in the crowd&quot; or &quot;Quick change&quot;.<br /> 2. &quot;Like the movies&quot; kind of works perfectly for this with enough imagination.<br /> 3. A good roll on &quot;Combustion&quot; could make this happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T19:37:08-08:00","id":793896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/793401-sfx-help?p=793507#post793507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b><u>Blink of the Eye</u></b> (Mundane): The Demon exploit quantum uncertainty to change their location from one unobserved spot to another.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this embed, lots of potential for ditching pursuit without being anywhere as dramatic as 4 Minutes Ago or other Exploits. Might I suggest that is the the Demon is being watched, they have a choice: Terminate the embed, and loose access to it for the scene; or continue the Embed and force the . They know that they're being watched, and that collapses their quantum position to a single possibility, not unlike how In My Pocket doesn't work if the character is searched. They need to wait a bit for their &quot;account lock-out&quot; to expire. Alternately, if they force the embed, it operates, but runs the risk of alerting the G-m.<br /> <br /> I thought about Combustion, but the embed requires that the demon fling a light match (or equivalent) to ignite something. I hesitant to expand an existing embed for fear of a rules-twinking player (all of mine) simply walking into a building and igniting all the paper in the area.<br /> <br /> In retrospect, I realize that Trick of the Light would work perfectly for making a person <i>think</i> that 1 or 2 had taken effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 12-28-2015, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T04:29:58-08:00","id":794088,"title":"","content":"Funny you mention Trick of the Light: After playing Guild Wars 2, I had the idea of Combining Blink of the Eye + Trick of the Light into an Interlock that lets you swap positions (even while observed) with an illusionary copy of you created with TotL (Justifying it as: observers don't know which one is the <i>real</i> you).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T08:07:09-08:00","id":794191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/793401-sfx-help#post793401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need help finding embeds that mechanically accomplish some of the classic espionage-thriller storybeats.<ul><li>You spot someone across the street, watching you. A bus drives past, obscuring your vision for a few seconds. Then, they're gone.</li> <li>You chase a person to a roof edge... and they throw themselves from the edge, as you rush to the edge, they're gone, and the people below are walking by obliviously, no sign of a splattered body, no one clinging to the wall.</li> <li>Someone walks into a dark church. All the candles in the place flicker to life.</li> </ul><br /> I'd prefer embeds to exploits or form-powers, as my chronicle already has a bit of a running gag that 4 Minutes Ago accomplishes everything. If there's no alternative option, eh, I'll live.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First one is easy that would be the <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Lost in the Crowd Embed: Enables the demon to remain perfectly undetectable by mundane means so long as they hide in a crowd of at least ten people.<br /> <br /> Second one could also be lost in the crowd but also the </span></span>Propulsion<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> demon form Teleportation with maybe the embeds <br /> Without a Trace: Vaporizes all physical traces of the demon from a scene.<br /> <br /> Using these two would make the person vanish and all physical evidence of them vanish also.<br /> <br /> That could be a emanation glitch maybe minor or major that causes that. Also the Combustion embed might do it being it causes things to blow up or catch fire. I would say use a gadget that has an are of affect that turns on any light source near the gadget when its turned on. </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T02:20:48-08:00","id":801232,"title":"","content":"I hope that helps","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}